doc Shift-right assignment: x >>= y, short for x = x >> y.
  ```
  let n = -16
  n >>= 2
  print n           // -4
  ```

  The left side can be any place of type `int`: a variable, a field, a
  slice element or `*p`, evaluated once.

needs std/let std/addr std/deref std/assign std/shr
syntax statement
  {x: place int} >>= {y: expr int}
expand
  let {$p} = &{x}
  *{$p} = *{$p} >> {y}
